// tools.memql -- the tools of an email composition run.
//
// A composition runs whole in Claude Code as the per-user email composer agent
// (role specialist), and these three tools are the ones it is given: read the
// context, render a composition until it reads right, submit it. Each is a
// builtin of the campaigns integration (component/campaigns/compose_tools.go).
//
// templateId and goalId are @autoInjected on every one: the run stamps the
// template it writes and its own goal, and the central validator drops any value
// the model supplies, so a session only ever writes its own template, and only
// while its own run is the composition that is writing. The session never sends a whole
// document, only a composition; the server rebuilds the email from the layout
// and the organization's brand kit, so the brand's pictures never pass through
// the model.

/// Start here, once. Answers the email you are writing and what you write it from:
/// the layout's blocks in order (id, type, role, sizes and example words), the
/// optional blocks you may drop, the repeatable blocks with how many copies they
/// allow, the content slots you write to, the brand slots the organization's kit
/// fills (never write into a brand block), the description of the email, the
/// organization's name, and the material: every file by its name in your workspace,
/// every picture with its handle, type, bytes and size, the picture of the finished
/// email (reference: guidance for the content and its order, not a picture for the
/// email unless the description asks for it), the files left out and why, and how
/// many pictures and bytes the brand leaves for yours. Then read the text files in
/// your workspace and use their words word for word, look at the pictures and the
/// reference, write a composition and check it with emailComposeRender.
@handler(type="function", name="campaignComposeContext")
@requiresAgentRole("specialist")
@executionTime("fast")
tool emailComposeContext {
  templateId  string  @autoInjected @description("The template this composition writes. Server-stamped by the composition run; the central validator drops any value the model supplies.")
  goalId      string  @autoInjected @description("The goal of the composition run. Server-stamped by the run; the central validator drops any value the model supplies.")
}

/// Check a composition without saving it. Send {subject, preheader, content, drop,
/// repeat}: content is a list of {id, text, label, href, alt, image} for the content
/// slots (text for heading, text and highlight blocks; label and href for buttons;
/// image, alt and href for pictures, where image is a picture's handle); drop lists
/// the optional blocks to leave out; repeat says how many copies of a repeatable
/// block to make, named id, id-2, id-3 and so on. Keep every link tag such as
/// {{confirmUrl}} as the layout has it, and leave a link empty when the material
/// gives none. Answers the subject, the HTML with each picture shown as its handle,
/// the plain text, the issues (code, block, message) and the slots the composition
/// writes. Fix what the issues say and what differs from the reference picture, and
/// render again: at most five renders in all. Then submit with emailComposeSubmit.
@handler(type="function", name="campaignComposeRender")
@requiresAgentRole("specialist")
@executionTime("fast")
tool emailComposeRender {
  templateId   string  @autoInjected @description("The template this composition writes. Server-stamped by the composition run; the central validator drops any value the model supplies.")
  goalId       string  @autoInjected @description("The goal of the composition run. Server-stamped by the run; the central validator drops any value the model supplies.")
  composition  object! @description("{subject, preheader, content: [{id, text, label, href, alt, image}], drop: [id], repeat: {id: copies}}. Pictures are named by handle. Never a whole email document.")
}

/// Save the composition as the template's draft and finish. Send the composition you
/// last rendered, never a whole document. Issues you could not fix within five
/// renders may stay: the draft lists them, and a person fixes them and publishes it.
/// Nothing here publishes. Call it once, at the end. Answers {templateId, revision,
/// issues}.
@handler(type="function", name="campaignComposeSubmit")
@requiresAgentRole("specialist")
@executionTime("fast")
tool emailComposeSubmit {
  templateId   string  @autoInjected @description("The template this composition writes. Server-stamped by the composition run; the central validator drops any value the model supplies.")
  goalId       string  @autoInjected @description("The goal of the composition run. Server-stamped by the run; the central validator drops any value the model supplies.")
  composition  object! @description("The composition last rendered: {subject, preheader, content, drop, repeat}, as emailComposeRender takes it.")
}
